1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"phase-4--4a-preparing-for-output","kind":"phase-article","route":"/roadmap/phase-4/4a-preparing-for-output","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/phase-4/4a-preparing-for-output","sourceHash":"5555a6d7ca9db053a59dbc8615daf937046ecdd052cc3e835f87bc2ab7f58d8b","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:53.445Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"4A — Preparing for Output","zh":"4A — 准备输出"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"what-youre-doing","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What You're Doing","zh":"你正在做什么"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You're ready to start speaking — your comprehension is strong and you understand native speakers in real conversation. But you've never actually produced this language before. Your mouth hasn't formed these sounds, your brain hasn't had to retrieve words under time pressure, and your speech muscles aren't trained for it.","zh":"你已经准备好开始说话了——你的理解能力很强，也能听懂真实对话中的母语者。但你实际上还从未用这门语言进行过输出。你的嘴巴还没有形成这些声音，大脑还没有在时间压力下提取词语，发声肌肉也尚未接受相应训练。"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This short sub-phase is about building the physical and mental foundation for speaking before jumping into conversations. It's preparation, not avoidance — you'll be producing the language every day, just not in conversation yet.","zh":"这一短暂的子阶段旨在让你在投入对话之前，为口语建立身体和心理基础。这是准备，而不是逃避——你每天都会输出这门语言，只是暂时还不会在对话中输出。"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The transition from input to output can feel uncomfortable. After hundreds of hours of understanding so much, suddenly struggling to say basic things is jarring. Push through it. The discomfort fades quickly with daily practice.","zh":"从输入转向输出可能会让人感到不适。经过数百小时的理解后，突然发现自己连简单的事情都说得很困难，会让人感到不习惯。坚持下去。这种不适会随着每天的练习迅速消退。"}},{"id":"whats-new","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What's New","zh":"有什么新内容"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Chorusing</strong> — Take a short audio clip (3-15 seconds) and repeat it over and over until you sound like the speaker. This trains pronunciation, rhythm, intonation, and speech muscles all at once. It feels awkward at first, but it's one of the most effective speaking exercises available. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/chorusing\">Chorusing</a>","zh":"<strong>跟读</strong>——选取一小段音频（3—15秒），反复跟读，直到听起来像原说话者。这会同时训练发音、节奏、语调和发声肌肉。起初会觉得很别扭，但这是现有最有效的口语练习之一。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/chorusing\">跟读</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Uncorrected Reading Aloud</strong> — Find a text in your target language and read it out loud. No feedback, no correction — just practice getting words from the page through your mouth. This builds fluency of articulation and helps you get comfortable with the physical sensation of speaking. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/uncorrected-reading-aloud\">Uncorrected Reading Aloud</a>","zh":"<strong>未经纠正的朗读</strong>——找一篇目标语言的文章并大声朗读。不需要反馈，也不需要纠正——只需练习把页面上的文字通过嘴说出来。这能提升发音流畅度，并帮助你适应开口说话时的身体感受。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/uncorrected-reading-aloud\">未经纠正的朗读</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Monologuing</strong> — Speak by yourself about anything. Narrate what you're doing, describe your day, react to a video, or just talk about whatever comes to mind. The goal is to practice retrieving words and forming sentences without the pressure of a listener. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/monologuing\">Monologuing</a>","zh":"<strong>独白练习</strong>——独自谈论任何话题。叙述你正在做的事，描述你的一天，对视频做出反应，或者想到什么就说什么。目标是在没有听众压力的情况下，练习提取词汇并组织句子。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/monologuing\">独白练习</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Output enters your routine.</strong> For the first time, your daily schedule now includes dedicated output time. This is a new pillar alongside priming, interactive, and freeflow. Don't neglect your input — you still need lots of listening and reading to keep growing — but output is now a daily commitment.","zh":"<strong>输出融入你的日常安排。</strong>从现在起，你的日程中首次加入了专门的输出时间。这与预热、互动式沉浸和自由流沉浸并列，成为新的支柱。不要忽视输入——你仍然需要大量听力和阅读来持续进步——但输出现在也成了每天必须完成的任务。"}},{"id":"your-routine","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Your Routine","zh":"你的日常安排"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Output takes about 20% of your time, with input still dominating: <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">The Pillars of Language Learning</a>","zh":"输出约占你时间的20%，输入仍占主导地位：<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">语言学习的支柱</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<strong>Priming:</strong> 10%","zh":"<strong>预热：</strong>10%"},{"en":"<strong>Interactive Immersion:</strong> 30%","zh":"<strong>互动式沉浸：</strong>30%"},{"en":"<strong>Freeflow Immersion:</strong> 40%","zh":"<strong>自由流沉浸：</strong>40%"},{"en":"<strong>Output:</strong> 20%","zh":"<strong>输出：</strong>20%"}]},{"id":"sample-daily-schedule","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"Sample Daily Schedule","zh":"每日安排示例"}},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Vocab study: 10 mins","zh":"词汇学习：10分钟"},{"en":"Interactive Reading/Listening: 30 mins","zh":"互动式阅读/听力：30分钟"},{"en":"Freeflow Listening: 40 mins","zh":"自由流听力：40分钟"},{"en":"Chorusing: 10 mins","zh":"跟读练习：10分钟"},{"en":"Uncorrected Reading Aloud: 10 mins","zh":"未经纠正的朗读：10分钟"}]},{"id":"when-to-move-on","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Move On","zh":"何时进入下一阶段"}},{"id":"segment-0016","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Move to 4B when you:","zh":"满足以下条件后进入4B："}},{"id":"segment-0017","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Can record a 5-minute monologue about a familiar topic (it doesn't need to be pretty)","zh":"能够围绕熟悉的话题录制5分钟的独白（不必说得漂亮）"},{"en":"Can read aloud for at least 10 minutes without your mouth becoming too sore or fatigued","zh":"能够连续朗读至少10分钟，且嘴巴不会过于酸痛或疲劳"}]},{"id":"research-and-reasoning","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Research and Reasoning","zh":"研究与依据"}},{"id":"segment-0019","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Chorusing, the core technique in this phase, draws on <a href=\"http://olle-kjellin.com/SpeechDoctor/ProcLP98.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Kjellin's (1998)</a> work on pronunciation as a motor skill. His approach — looping and repeating short audio clips to match native-speaker pronunciation — develops prosody (rhythm and intonation) and articulation simultaneously by leveraging the auditory system to guide the speech organs toward correct production. This combines perception and production practice in ways that conscious attention to individual sounds often fails to achieve.","zh":"跟读练习是本阶段的核心技巧，其依据来自<a href=\"http://olle-kjellin.com/SpeechDoctor/ProcLP98.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Kjellin（1998）</a>关于将发音视为运动技能的研究。他的方法是循环播放并重复短音频片段，以匹配母语者的发音；借助听觉系统引导发音器官正确发音，同时发展韵律（节奏和语调）与发音能力。这种方式将感知与产出练习结合起来，而单纯有意识地关注单个音素往往无法达到同样的效果。"}}],"cards":[]}}]
